# Shared cloud database (optional).
#
# Leave these unset and TeamFlow stores the workspace locally in the browser
# (AsyncStorage) — useful for a solo demo, but nothing is shared between people.
#
# Set both and the exact same screens read/write a shared Postgres database
# through its PostgREST-style Data API, so every teammate opening the live link
# sees the same projects, tasks, comments, team members and activity. Apply db/schema.sql to
# the database first. These are build-time public values (EXPO_PUBLIC_*), so use
# a Data API endpoint whose anonymous role is meant to be reachable from a
# browser — never put a Postgres connection string or a secret key here.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DATA_API_URL=https://<your-endpoint>.apirest.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb/rest/v1
EXPO_PUBLIC_DATA_API_AUTH_URL=https://<your-endpoint>.neonauth.<region>.aws.neon.tech/neondb/auth
